Second iteration informed by Anthropic's "Effective context engineering for
AI agents" (smallest set of high-signal tokens, just-in-time over preloading,
canonical examples over exhaustive rules).

CLAUDE.md (55 -> 29 lines):
- drop the "building-block skills" table (each skill already carries its own
  description in the system prompt — the table was duplicate metadata)
- drop the workflow tables; replace with a single canonical worked example
- move Maintenance + Scripts CLI sections to REFERENCE.md (on-demand, not
  auto-loaded)
- add an explicit "externalize state on long sessions" rule pointing at
  .claude/notes/<feature>.md
- add a "just-in-time over preloading" rule

REFERENCE.md: new file, on-demand only. Holds Maintenance, Scripts CLI, RTK
meta commands, and the notes convention. CLAUDE.md does NOT auto-import it.

settings.json:
- disable claude-md-management plugin (overlaps the built-in update-config
  skill that's already loaded by the harness)

Skill body trims (no behavior change, denser prose):
- discovery: collapse the redundant Decision Tree (the bullets above already
  describe the same triage)
- architecture: tighten the Auto-deepen paragraph
- define: tighten the research-team / gate-rule paragraph
- build: replace the inline 5-question verification check with a pointer to
  superpowers:verification-before-completion (the canonical version)
